    "When you say \"total overtime hours per month for the entire workforce cannot exceed 20 hours per worker,\" do you mean each individual worker can work at most 20 overtime hours in a month (so total overtime is capped at 20 × number of workers that month), or is there a single company-wide cap of 20 total overtime hours per month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the interpretation of the overtime cap, presenting two mutually exclusive options for one constraint."
}

